@* Bundles the order-critical <head> stylesheet stack every host App.razor
   otherwise hand-types with its own "ORDER MATTERS" comment (DESIGN.md §3):
   self-hosted fonts → Radzen's material-base → design tokens (must load
   AFTER Radzen, so its remaps win) → the host's own app-specific stylesheet,
   then theme.js, which applies the stored light/dark preference before first
   paint. Drop it once near the top of the host's <head>, in place of the
   five hand-typed tags.

   Renders as plain <link>/<script> tags via static SSR — App.razor is never
   itself an interactive component, so this needs no @rendermode and works
   the same way the existing <ResourcePreloader /> already does inside
   <head>. It only owns the four order-dependent tags: a host's own isolated
   CSS bundle (*.styles.css) and body-script ordering (nav.js before
   blazor.web.js) are unrelated ordering constraints left for the host, as
   documented on the PR. *@

<link rel="stylesheet" href="_content/AndreGoepel.Design.Blazor/css/fonts.css" />
<link rel="stylesheet" href="_content/Radzen.Blazor/css/material-base.css" />
<link rel="stylesheet" href="_content/AndreGoepel.Design.Blazor/css/design.css" />
<link rel="stylesheet" href="@AppStylesheetHref" />
<script src="_content/AndreGoepel.Design.Blazor/js/theme.js"></script>

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// The host's own app-specific stylesheet href, e.g. <c>@@Assets["app.css"]</c>.
    /// Loaded last in the ordering-critical stack, after the design tokens.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public string AppStylesheetHref { get; set; } = "";
}
